GNU m4 for OpenVMS
==================

This is GNU m4 @VERSION@ built natively for OpenVMS @ARCH@, from the
unmodified GNU release plus the patches in the vms-m4 project:

    https://github.com/issinoho/vms-m4

Kit version: @KITVERSION@.  m4 is free software under the GNU General Public
License, version 3 or later; see COPYING.  The manual is M4.TXT; M4.1 is the
manual page.  GNU Bison for OpenVMS uses this m4.

What is installed
-----------------
    M4$ROOT:[BIN]M4.EXE              m4
    M4$ROOT:[000000]M4$SETUP.COM     defines the m4 command
    M4$ROOT:[DOC]                    this file, COPYING, NEWS, M4.TXT, M4.1
    SYS$STARTUP:M4$STARTUP.COM       defines M4$ROOT

Setting up
----------
The kit installs M4$STARTUP.COM into SYS$STARTUP and runs it once.  To
define M4$ROOT at every boot, the system manager adds this line to
SYS$MANAGER:SYSTARTUP_VMS.COM:

    $ @SYS$STARTUP:M4$STARTUP.COM

Each user (or SYLOGIN.COM, for everyone) then defines the command:

    $ @M4$ROOT:[000000]M4$SETUP.COM

syscmd and esyscmd
------------------
syscmd and esyscmd run their command as DCL in a subprocess (LIB$SPAWN),
with the output collected in a temporary file in SYS$SCRATCH; the
subprocess has your symbols and logical names:

    syscmd(`directory/size *.c')
    esyscmd(`write sys$output f$getsyi("NODENAME")')

syscmd's output goes to m4's output in sequence.  sysval is 0 after a
command that succeeded; after one that failed it is the exit code of a C
program that exited with a POSIX status, otherwise the severity of the VMS
status (2 error, 4 fatal, 0 warning).

Upper-case options and batch jobs
---------------------------------
Under the TRADITIONAL DCL parse style DCL upper-cases the unquoted parts of
a command and the C run-time library passes them to m4 in lower case, so an
unquoted -D (define) arrives as -d (debug).  Batch jobs use TRADITIONAL
even when interactive logins are set to EXTENDED.  Quote the options that
use capital letters ("-DNAME=value"), or start the procedure with

    $ SET PROCESS/PARSE_STYLE=EXTENDED

Exit status
-----------
Under DCL a failed run exits with an error-severity status, so ON ERROR and
IF .NOT. $STATUS work; m4's exit code N is ($STATUS .AND. %X7F8) / 8.
Under a GNV shell, $? is the exit code as on Unix.
